/T (The most useful high-level model is a distributed architecture with many independently owned services rather than a simple two-tier website. Public Amazon engineering material describes thousands of services and core systems that support Amazon Stores. In a microservices design, each service focuses on a business capability and can be deployed or scaled separately. Amazon's exact service boundaries and the complete Amazon.com production topology are not public, so this report uses a representative architecture.)
/E (The most useful high-level model is a distributed architecture with many independently owned services rather than a simple two-tier website. Public Amazon engineering material describes thousands of services and core systems that support Amazon Stores. In a microservices design, each service focuses on a business capability and can be deployed or scaled separately. Amazon's exact service boundaries and the complete Amazon.com production topology are not public, so this report uses a representative architecture.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
