130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (Caching stores frequently requested content or computed results closer to where they are needed. A cache can reduce response time, backend load and cost, but it introduces trade-offs: stale data, cache misses, invalidation and the possibility that a cold or unavailable cache sends too much traffic to the underlying database. Amazon's Builders' Library explicitly discusses these challenges and recommends measuring cache hit rate, selecting expiration policies deliberately, monitoring cache health and ensuring services remain resilient when a cache is unavailable.)
/E (Caching stores frequently requested content or computed results closer to where they are needed. A cache can reduce response time, backend load and cost, but it introduces trade-offs: stale data, cache misses, invalidation and the possibility that a cold or unavailable cache sends too much traffic to the underlying database. Amazon's Builders' Library explicitly discusses these challenges and recommends measuring cache hit rate, selecting expiration policies deliberately, monitoring cache health and ensuring services remain resilient when a cache is unavailable.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (A content delivery network \(CDN\) is especially useful for static assets such as images, stylesheets, scripts and other cacheable content. Edge delivery brings content closer to users and can reduce origin traffic. AWS documentation describes CloudFront as a CDN and shows how it can cache static content, while a web application firewall can help protect the public entry point. These are established AWS design patterns; they should not be presented as proof that every Amazon.com request follows the exact reference design.)
/E (A content delivery network \(CDN\) is especially useful for static assets such as images, stylesheets, scripts and other cacheable content. Edge delivery brings content closer to users and can reduce origin traffic. AWS documentation describes CloudFront as a CDN and shows how it can cache static content, while a web application firewall can help protect the public entry point. These are established AWS design patterns; they should not be presented as proof that every Amazon.com request follows the exact reference design.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
