/T (Amazon.com is operated by Amazon as a global service. AWS is Amazon's cloud-computing business, but it is important not to assume that every Amazon.com production component is simply hosted as a customer workload on public AWS. Amazon has operated large-scale infrastructure and data centres, and public sources do not provide a complete map of which retail components run on which infrastructure. A careful report should say that Amazon operates its own global infrastructure and uses a broad internal platform; exact placement of every Amazon.com component is not fully public.)
/E (Amazon.com is operated by Amazon as a global service. AWS is Amazon's cloud-computing business, but it is important not to assume that every Amazon.com production component is simply hosted as a customer workload on public AWS. Amazon has operated large-scale infrastructure and data centres, and public sources do not provide a complete map of which retail components run on which infrastructure. A careful report should say that Amazon operates its own global infrastructure and uses a broad internal platform; exact placement of every Amazon.com component is not fully public.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
