293 0 obj
<<
/Title (Amazon.com illustrates why large e-commerce platforms are better understood as distributed systems than as a single web server connected to one database. Separating business capabilities can support targeted scaling, independent releases and fault isolation. Caching, edge delivery, monitoring and workload isolation help improve performance and reliability, but each adds design and operational trade-offs. Because Amazon's complete internal implementation is proprietary, the strongest case study combines verified public statements with clearly labelled conceptual architecture rather than guessing exact servers or frameworks.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 253 0 R
>>
endobj
