388 0 obj
<<
/Title (The most useful high-level model is a distributed architecture with many independently owned services rather than a simple two-tier website. Public Amazon engineering material describes thousands of services and core systems that support Amazon Stores. In a microservices design, each service focuses on a business capability and can be deployed or scaled separately. Amazon's exact service boundaries and the complete Amazon.com production topology are not public, so this report uses a representative architecture.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 362 0 R
/First 399 0 R
/Last 400 0 R
/Count -7
/Next 389 0 R
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Title (Request flow: a customer opens Amazon.com; DNS and edge delivery route the request; web/API entry points send it to the relevant business service; the service reads or updates data and may communicate with other services; the response returns to the customer. Asynchronous events can support downstream work such as notifications, analytics or fulfilment workflows.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 362 0 R
/Prev 388 0 R
>>
endobj
