392 0 obj
<<
/Title (Amazon's public engineering material shows a broad, evolving technology environment rather than a single language or framework for the entire retail site. The eCommerce Foundation organisation says it operates core systems, infrastructure and services used by teams across Amazon Stores. Public documentation also describes AWS building blocks commonly used for e-commerce systems, including APIs, compute services, databases, caching and event-driven integrations. The precise language/framework mix for each Amazon.com service is not fully disclosed in one official public inventory.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 366 0 R
/Next 393 0 R
>>
